.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt VT05 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vt05 ,
.Nm vt50 ,
.Nm vt52 ,
.Nm dp3300 ,
.Nm gecon ,
.Nm dm2500
.Nd emulators of classic serial terminals
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 2Bfr
.Op Fl b Ar baudrate
.Ar command Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These programs each emulate a classic serial character terminal.
On startup they create a pseudo-terminal, run
.Ar command
attached to it, and render the terminal output in an SDL window
using a period-correct character set with phosphor glow and
scanline effects.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Nm vt05
DEC VT05, 72x20 characters.
.It Nm vt50
DEC VT50, 80x12 characters.
.It Nm vt52
DEC VT52, 80x24 characters.
.It Nm dp3300
DP3300 terminal, 72x25 characters.
.It Nm gecon
GECON console, 46x26 characters.
.It Nm dm2500
Datamedia Elite 2500, 80x24 characters.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar baudrate
Emulate the given line speed in bits per second.
.It Fl B
Send rubout (0x7F) instead of backspace when the backspace key
is pressed.
.It Fl f
Start in fullscreen mode.
.It Fl r
Rerun
.Ar command
when it exits.
.It Fl 2
Scale the window by an extra factor of two.
.It Fl a
Only for
.Nm dp3300 :
use the TMS4100 character set instead of the default one.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run
.Xr sh 1
on an emulated VT05 at 9600 baud:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
vt05 -b 9600 sh
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xterm 1
